==Trivia==
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Raiden was a part of two other [[Cat Combo]]s: [[Overhaul (Removed Combo)|Overhaul]] and [[Dragon Emperors (Removed Combo)|Dragon Emperors]].
*Prior to [[Version 14.3 Update|Version 14.3]], God-Emperor Raiden was one of the few [[:Category:Cats with Ultra Talents|Cats with Ultra Talents]] to lack a second [[Talent Orbs|Talent Orb]] slot.
*God-Emperor Raiden's Behemoth Slayer Ultra [[Talents|Talent]], added in the same update as [[Ensanglion the Calamity]], may imply that Raiden was built specifically to fight Ensanglion in the event of his return.
**Further supporting this is that Raiden, [[Ganglion (Uber Rare Cat)|Ganglion]] and Ensanglion are all described as ancient in [[Nyanko Daisensou|BCJP]].
**Raiden is also described as "The ONLY Hope against ANCIENT CAT DRAGONS" in the [[Lords of Destruction DRAGON EMPERORS (Gacha Event)|Lords of Destruction DRAGON EMPERORS]]' poster.
*Raiden is the first Dragon Emperor to be called a "machine" and "ancient weapon" in BCJP, the second being [[Vornado (Uber Rare Cat)|Vornado]]. Both are also [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|anti-Red]], and with God-Emperor Raiden's Ultra Talents, both are immune to [[Surge Attack|Surge]].
**Raiden and Vornado are two of the three Dragon Emperors units that aren't dragons. The third is [[Vars (Uber Rare Cat)|Vars]], a knight riding an unnamed dragon.
*''Raiden'' (雷電) is a Japanese word meaning "thunder and lightning".
*Since several of the other Dragon Emperors appear to have been named after video games, this unit may be referencing the vertical shoot 'em up arcade game ''[[wikipedia:Raiden (video game)|Raiden]]''.

